  ],
  "text": "Divers pulled a corroded lump off a shipwreck. Inside it were thirty bronze gears. Nobody was building gearing like that again for well over a thousand years. It is a calculator, and what it calculates is the sky. Turn the handle and it shows you where the sun and moon are going to be. It predicts eclipses. It tracks the four year cycle of the games. It even models the moon speeding up and slowing down across its orbit. Which raises the obvious question. What happened next? Nothing. Nobody built on it. The knowledge went into the sea and stayed there. Progress is not a line. Things get invented, then lost, and stay lost for centuries. Whoever made this had no idea they were the end of it. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
